body:
Unfortunately, I haven't been able to reproduce this on a Meta Quest 3 (deploying from a Linux desktop, although, I'm not sure that would have any impact on the test) using Godot 4.4-stable.

I first tried making my own test project which followed the instructions in the OP. I used GDScript for the XR, but just added a node with the following C# script attached to make sure C# was there and working:

```C#
using Godot;
using System;

public partial class CSharpTest : Node
{
	public override void _Ready()
	{
		GD.Print("Hello from C#");
    }
}
```

I tried running that 3-4 times on the Quest and didn't get any crashes.

Then I downloaded the MRP and tried running that 10 times in a row (I counted!) and it never crashed for me.

Is there anything else necessary to get the crash?

Also, I don't know if this has any effect on anything, but what version of the .NET SDK are using on your desktop? I've got `8.0.114`
